From ac6df86e63287d2fce1e4d85beb350952c2ca1ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:46:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH v3 6/7] mailbox: sun55i: Add KUnit tests

Add 26 KUnit tests for the sun55i message box driver. They run the
channel operations and the interrupt handler against a fake register
bank in plain memory: channel-to-route mapping, sending on all 12
channels, last_tx_done() and peek_data() against the FIFO count,
startup and shutdown flushing bounded by the FIFO depth, write IRQ
threshold and status handling, and the interrupt handler (spurious
and disabled-channel interrupts, empty FIFOs, several channels and
routes at once, drain bounded by the FIFO depth, no crosstalk between
channels).

The driver accesses the fake registers with readl() and writel(), which
are not guaranteed to work on plain memory on every architecture, so
the tests depend on ARM64 or COMPILE_TEST.
---
 drivers/mailbox/Kconfig              |  12 +
 drivers/mailbox/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/mailbox/sun55i_msgbox_test.c | 764 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 777 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/mailbox/sun55i_msgbox_test.c

